      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point -- We do know why we\u0027re starting up via system_get_reset_flags(). There are quite a few reset causes where it seems we\u0027d want to run this, though, so it might be easiest to skip this if RESET_FLAG_SYSJUMP is set, rather than white listing the valid causes. I made that change in the follow-up patch set and it seemed to do the trick.\n\nI think the caller wants to call power_on() after sysjump since, for better or worse, we do quite a bit of work in this function aside from just bringing up power (setting ap_on, enabling charger interrupt, calling hooks, etc). But since PMIC_PWRON_L seems to be the only outlier case, I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s worth making changes elsewhere to get around this outlier case.",
